{
  "comment": "default preserves immediate aimbody behavior; smooth treats camera look as a wish direction and smoothly moves the body and configured limbs toward it; physical runs the body as an active ragdoll during normal play (torso tethered to the movement root, head+torso receive look torque, limbs inherit through joints); hybrid does that but also springs limbs toward the procedural animation pose so it follows animations/weapons while carrying momentum. All physical tuning is in ragdoll.json physical.*. World Z is vertical and body yaw rotates around world Z. smoothingFactor 1.0 is approximately a 250 ms response; larger values are slower and smaller values are faster. Smooth mode never snaps. For each limb, gains scale camera look pitch into local pitch/yaw/roll rotations (default/smooth only). Camera sway is configured separately in camconfig.json.",
  "enabled": true,
  // "enabled": false,
  // "mode": "default",
  "mode": "hybrid", 
  // In hybrid body mode: "default" makes only the arms use the normal
  // aimbody pose; "hybrid" keeps the arms physically blended too.
  "arms_mode": "hybrid",
  // "arms_mode": "default",
  // Hold RMB to physically move the right arm's center toward this player-
  // local point, then aim the weapon along camera forward. X=forward,
  // Y=lateral, Z=up. Change Y for left/right and Z for height.
  "right_arm_pointing": {
    "mode": "rmb",
    "center_offset": [2.0, 0.0, 1.7],
    // Arm-local goal correction in degrees: [pitch, yaw, roll].
    // Use this to correct an avatar whose centered arm points down/up.
    "rotation_degrees": [85.0, -90.0, 0.0],
    // Higher is a faster but still smooth enter/return transition.
    "blend_rate": 25.0,
    // 1.0 = loose/current behavior. 10.0 = ten times stronger target
    // correction and settling against movement/external disturbances.
    // "aim_strength": 5.0,
    // "aim_strength": 1.0,
    // "aim_strength": 20.0,
    // "aim_strength": 99.0,
    // "aim_strength": 999.0,
    "aim_strength": 10.0,
    // "aim_strength": 7.0,
    // Higher values make the arm catch up more calmly instead of whipping.
    "follow_damping": 1.0,
    // Angular-speed ceiling for aiming correction (radians per second).
    "max_follow_speed": 30.0,
    "fov": {
      // "enabled": true,
      "enabled": false,
      "multiplier": 0.5,
      "duration": 0.5,
      "easing": "ease_in_out"
    }
  },
